import html,json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
sources=json.loads((ROOT/'data/sources.json').read_text())
pages={
'methodology':('Methodology & limitations',"""
<p>IndicEval v0.1 is a research preview for single-turn coding and reasoning capabilities. It evaluates outputs from agent backends; it does not measure autonomous planning, tool use, or repository-level engineering.</p>
<h2>200 tasks, four sourced strata</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Track</th><th>Language</th><th>Tasks</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Python code generation</td><td>Hinglish</td><td>50</td><td>HumanEval adaptations</td></tr><tr><td>Mathematical reasoning</td><td>Hindi</td><td>50</td><td>NVIDIA GSM8K-Hi</td></tr><tr><td>Causal reasoning</td><td>Tamil</td><td>50</td><td>XCOPA</td></tr><tr><td>Reading comprehension</td><td>Bengali</td><td>50</td><td>IndicGenBench XQuAD-IN</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>The first 50 source records are used for code, math and causal reasoning. Reading uses the first 50 records whose accepted answers all occur verbatim in the supplied context. Excluded source IDs are recorded in <a href="https://github.com/SayedZahur786/indiceval/blob/main/data/exclusions.json">the exclusion ledger</a>. This is a convenience sample, not a random or representative sample.</p>
<h2>Review status is explicit</h2><p>150 tasks retain the original source's documented human translation/review evidence. We verify reference execution, arithmetic annotations, source-label fidelity and answer spans. These checks are not an independent human adjudication of every answer.</p><p>The 50 Hinglish coding prompts are new adaptations of human-written English problems. Their reference solutions pass the original tests, but the Hinglish language adaptations require independent review. <strong>This is not a fully hand-checked 200-task release.</strong> Review evidence is visible in each task.</p>
<h2>Scoring contracts</h2><ul><li><strong>Code:</strong> complete Python code, optionally inside one Python code fence, passes the upstream tests in an unprivileged Docker container. Network disabled, no host mounts, read-only root, bounded CPU, memory, process count, output and execution time.</li><li><strong>Math:</strong> a single finite number, compared using decimal arithmetic. Unicode digits and whitespace are normalized. Explanations and units fail the specified format.</li><li><strong>Causal:</strong> exactly 1 or 2 after whitespace and Unicode normalization, matched to the source label.</li><li><strong>Reading:</strong> normalized exact match to any accepted reference. Case and punctuation are preserved. Semantically valid paraphrases can be marked wrong.</li></ul>
<h2>Metrics and repetitions</h2><p>Accuracy is the fraction of tasks passed by the first sample, averaged across repetitions. pass@k uses 1 − C(n−c,k) / C(n,k), averaged over task/repetition groups, where n is samples and c is passing samples. k must not exceed n. See <a href="https://github.com/openai/human-eval/blob/master/human_eval/evaluation.py">the HumanEval estimator</a>.</p><p>At least two repetitions are required for submissions. Seeds vary by repeat and sample; a provider may ignore seed requests. We report each repetition's accuracy, sample variance (denominator R−1), and range. Variance is in squared proportion units. Two repeats are not a confidence interval and cannot establish ranking significance.</p><p>Latency measures each API request's wall time, including HTTP overhead, excluding local grading. p95 uses nearest-rank selection. Cost is an estimate from provider-reported prompt/completion tokens and user-declared prices per million tokens. Cost per task includes all n samples and is averaged over task/repetition groups. Missing token usage or pricing produces unknown total cost. Cached-token pricing, tool fees and local hardware cost are not estimated.</p><p>HTTP failures, malformed outputs, timeouts and wrong answers remain in the denominator. Requests are not automatically retried. An unavailable code sandbox aborts the run rather than creating a misleading score. Partial artifacts cannot pass submission validation.</p>
<h2>Contamination and comparison limits</h2><p>These are public benchmark derivatives. They may be in model training data, and the original HumanEval tests are widely exposed. We cannot certify contamination-free evaluation. Submitters must disclose known training exposure, retrieval, tools, prompt changes and model versions. Keep benchmark tasks out of training when reporting evaluation scores; licences may legally permit uses beyond this research recommendation.</p><p>Task type and language are completely coupled in this preview. A difference between Hindi and Tamil strata could be caused by task type, not language. Do not interpret the breakdowns as a controlled comparison of languages. English controls exist for the code stratum only and are not a second counted dataset.</p><p>Public tests do not establish exhaustive correctness or protect against deliberate test exploitation. Containers reduce execution risk but are not a hardened public multi-tenant service. Review untrusted submissions in a disposable environment. The static site never executes submitted code.</p>
<h2>Evidence and versioning</h2><p>Task hashes, dataset SHA-256, source revision IDs, raw samples and run settings are preserved. <a href="/data/manifest.json">Download the manifest</a> and <a href="https://github.com/SayedZahur786/indiceval/tree/main/docs/evidence">inspect verification evidence</a>. A reference-answer fixture validates plumbing, not model capability, and is excluded from rankings.</p>
<h2>Research context</h2><p>IndicEval builds on HumanEval, GSM8K-Hi, XCOPA and IndicGenBench. This independent project is not affiliated with <a href="https://github.com/telekom/IndicEval-XL">IndicEval-XL</a>, <a href="https://github.com/mrigankpawagi/HinglishEval">HinglishEval</a>, or other projects called IndicEval. No claim of scientific novelty or superior model performance is made.</p>
"""),
'privacy':('Privacy',"""
<p>Effective 19 November 2026. IndicEval is a static research website maintained through the <a href="https://github.com/SayedZahur786/indiceval">project repository</a>.</p>
<h2>Website use</h2><p>The site has no accounts, sign-in, payment flow, or database of uploaded reports. The report inspector reads your selected JSON file locally in browser memory. It does not upload the file. Search and filters are local and are not persisted.</p>
<h2>Analytics</h2><p>Vercel Web Analytics is wired for aggregate website traffic measurement. The client does not intentionally send task searches, report content, API keys or custom events. It skips loading analytics when your browser sends Do Not Track. Blocking analytics does not prevent use of the site. Vercel hosts the site and processes network requests and operational logs under its own policies. See <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy">Vercel's analytics privacy documentation</a>.</p>
<h2>External services</h2><p>Fonts are served by Google Fonts, which receives browser requests. GitHub and linked research sources have their own privacy practices. When you submit an issue or pull request, your GitHub identity and content may become public.</p>
<h2>Local evaluation</h2><p>The Python runner sends benchmark prompts to the endpoint you configure. That provider may process or retain them under its policies. API keys are read from an environment variable and are not written into run artifacts. Raw model responses and usage are stored locally in the output directory; review them before sharing. Never submit credentials, private prompts or personal data.</p>
<h2>Questions and removal requests</h2><p>Open a <a href="https://github.com/SayedZahur786/indiceval/issues">project issue</a> for public, non-sensitive questions. Do not include sensitive information in a public issue. Repository owners can review data correction/removal requests; third-party caches or forks are outside the project's control.</p>
"""),
'terms':('Terms of use',"""
<p>Effective 19 November 2026. IndicEval is an experimental, openly inspectable research tool. It is provided as-is without a guarantee of accuracy, availability, security or fitness for a particular use.</p>
<h2>Research use</h2><p>Scores describe performance on a small, public dataset under recorded conditions. They do not establish general intelligence, safety, reliability, cultural competence, or suitability for a consequential deployment. Do not represent fixture diagnostics as model results.</p>
<h2>Code and dataset rights</h2><p>Project code is MIT-licensed. Dataset records retain their individual upstream licences; the repository's code licence does not replace them. XQuAD-IN derivatives retain CC BY-SA 4.0. Consult the <a href="/sources.html">source and licence ledger</a> before redistribution. Attribution and licence notices must be preserved.</p>
<h2>Contributions</h2><p>Submit only content and run artifacts you are authorized to publish. Disclose benchmark exposure and evaluation settings. Do not include secrets or personal data. Submitting does not guarantee inclusion in the leaderboard. Maintainers may reject, correct or remove misleading, incomplete or unverifiable results. Corrections should be versioned and linked to their evidence.</p>
<h2>Local code execution</h2><p>The runner requires Docker for generated code. You control the endpoint, API charges and execution environment. Do not execute untrusted code directly on your host or grant the evaluation containers extra privileges. The public site does not provide hosted model execution.</p>
""")
}
items=[]
for key,s in sources.items():
    items.append('<h2>'+html.escape(key)+'</h2><p><strong>'+html.escape(s['authors'])+'</strong></p><p>Licence: '+html.escape(s['license'])+'. <a href="'+html.escape(s['url'])+'">Pinned source</a> · <a href="https://github.com/SayedZahur786/indiceval/blob/main/data/licenses/'+key+'.txt">Licence text</a></p><p>'+html.escape(s['review'])+'</p><p>'+html.escape(s['consent'])+'</p><p class="hash">Source revision: '+s['revision']+'</p>')
pages['sources']=('Sources, licences & consent','<p>Every task records its upstream item, immutable revision, licence and transformation. No forum content or private conversation is included. Published licences are the redistribution basis; they are not proof that individual participant consent records were audited by this project.</p>'+''.join(items)+"""
<h2>Changes and attribution</h2><p>HumanEval's first 50 tasks receive new Hinglish instructions while retaining signatures, helper code, canonical solutions and tests; original MIT notices remain. GSM8K-Hi questions and solutions are retained, with a numeric-answer format instruction and robust parsing of the final-answer marker. XCOPA Tamil premises, choices and labels are retained with a numbered response wrapper. XQuAD-IN Bengali contexts, questions and answers are retained with a short-answer instruction; only span-verifiable items are selected. XQuAD-IN adaptations remain CC BY-SA 4.0.</p>
<h2>Consent boundary</h2><p>No new participants were recruited and no private messages were collected. Upstream annotator consent paperwork is not available in these releases. If your launch policy requires that paperwork for every source, this release does not meet that gate. Source licensing and consent are recorded separately rather than conflated.</p>
<h2>Contamination marker</h2><p>The upstream canary is preserved in the <a href="/data/manifest.json">dataset manifest</a>. Published tasks and answers are downloadable for auditing. Do not treat public availability as evidence of contamination-free evaluation.</p>
<h2>Report an issue</h2><p>Use the task's source link and hash when reporting an answer, translation or rights issue in the <a href="https://github.com/SayedZahur786/indiceval/issues">repository</a>. Known limitations and corrections are versioned publicly.</p>
""")
for slug,(title,body) in pages.items():
    content=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{title} — IndicEval</title><meta name="description" content="{title} for the IndicEval research preview."><link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.css"><script defer src="/assets/analytics.js"></script></head><body><header><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="mark">इ</span>IndicEval</a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="/#explorer">Task explorer</a><a href="/methodology.html">Methodology</a><a href="/sources.html">Sources</a></nav><a class="repo" href="https://github.com/SayedZahur786/indiceval">GitHub</a></header><main class="prose"><div class="eyebrow">INDICEVAL / RESEARCH PREVIEW</div><h1>{title}</h1>{body}</main><footer><a href="/">IndicEval home</a><nav><a href="/privacy.html">Privacy</a><a href="/terms.html">Terms</a><a href="/sources.html">Licences</a></nav></footer></body></html>'''
    (ROOT/'site'/f'{slug}.html').write_text(content)
print('Policy and methodology pages built')
